Two targeted improvements, both cheap and additive to the existing pipeline:

1. **Exact parametric scan + local refinement of the two-heptagon family.** The best-known n=14 ratio configs are two staggered regular heptagons; a dense 3-parameter grid (latitude z, twist angle, plus unequal radii/heights variants) evaluated exactly, then locally refined by coordinate descent, seeds the annealer with near-optimal basins instead of hoping random restarts find them.

2. **Occasional large basin-hopping kicks.** Small kicks (0.006–0.012) can only refine within the current twist state; every 7th hop a large kick (0.05–0.1) allows crossing into a different twist/structure basin, which the low-sharpness re-anneal then reorders.

